<title>SRI LANKA: Commercial Bank shares leap five percent.</title>
<headline>Commercial Bank shares leap five percent.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Commercial Bank Ltd rose 5.4 percent, or five rupees, to 97 on local buying of 1,200 shares in late Friday morning trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The share is very good value at current levels because it rose to over 400 rupees when the market rallied in early 1994,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Commercial Bank is a blue chip and one of four private banks listed in Colombo.</p>
<p>A further quantity of 10,000 shares was on bid at 97.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
